## Version 8.5.6

- `qgis` and `qgisflat` layers have `withCache` off by default; cache settings of a `qgis` layer are passed on to its leaf layers
- `qgis` layer option `compositeRender` renamed to `withCompositeRender`
- QGIS: raster layer opacity is read from the renderer, opacity is no longer applied twice
- tile sources (WMTS, `tile` layers): a coarser source level is upscaled (up to ~1.6x) rather than a finer one downscaled, keeping labels readable
- Postgres table names with uppercase or special characters are quoted correctly
- OWS sources: new `token` authorization type, authorization options are validated
- client layer data is loaded directly instead of through a polled queue of 3 requests
- Python packages pinned to minor versions; the image is built from the pip lock file
- new `install/host_logging.sh` sets up rsyslog and logrotate on the Docker host

## Version 8.5.5

- QField Cloud: a push is applied in one transaction and rejected as a whole on error; deltas are stored for status queries, new `deltaLifeTime` option
- QField Cloud: model permissions, QGIS layer locks and read-only flags are respected
- QField Cloud: new `syncFiles` option sends file field content to QField
- QField Cloud: improved base map rendering, base map size is limited
- ALKIS: GeoInfoDok 7 is the default (`GWS_ALKIS_GID_VERSION` for version 6), house number range queries
- `server.timeZone` is ignored, the time zone is set by the `TZ` environment variable (image default `Europe/Berlin`)
- `server.preConfigure` and `server.postConfigure` removed
- default locale is `de_DE` (was `en_CA`)
- system CA certificate bundle is used for TLS; additional CA certificates via `GWS_EXTRA_CA_BUNDLE`
- LDAP: `memberOf` and `matches` rules are checked against the user entry only, login attribute is matched case-insensitively
- image formats: more predefined formats; new `mode`, `background` and `quality` options; faster PNG encoding; `name` must be a predefined format, custom format names are no longer accepted
- MIME types are normalized; WMS and QGIS sources are requested in the format matching the layer's `imageFormat`
- default rewrite rules are appended after the configured rules (were prepended)
- psycopg upgraded to v3
- plugin API: database connections use `begin`/`execute` with explicit transactions instead of `connect`/`exec`

## Version 8.5.4

- updated and restructured administrator documentation
- new developer documentation and Python API documentation
- new `mapshare` plugin: shareable links and QR codes for a map position
- QField Cloud: the GWS project is now optional, new `thumbnail` option, better error handling
- default reversed rewrite rules for the homepage and project pages
- `make.sh` can run in docker
- plugin API: `gws.base.shape` moved to `lib`; root lifecycle functions moved to the core API

## Version 8.5.3

- configuration warnings: non-fatal configuration problems are collected and logged in a warnings report after startup
- deprecated and ignored options now produce a configuration warning
- `gws` CLI commands run as the GWS user instead of root
- a layer whose extent cannot be determined is a configuration error (was a warning)
- `gws cache` CLI: new selection options `-bbox`, `-wkt` and `-levels` for `seed` and `drop`, `seed -maxAge` reseeds tiles older than the given duration
- new admin object inspector (`adminInspector`)
- improved reprojection of tile sources (WMTS, tile layers)
- reworked XML and GML serialization for OWS services
- plugin API: extension types are declared with class decorators
- updated demos

## Version 8.5.2

- base image upgraded to Ubuntu 26.04 (Python 3.14, GDAL 3.12, PROJ 9.7); all Python packages pinned to their current major versions
- bundled MapServer upgraded to 8.6.6, built with OGC API support; the build tarball is created locally by `install/image.py`
- `Application.register_supported_crs()` lets plugins add a CRS to the raster subsystem; QField projects register their QGIS CRS
- fixed: temporary layers (e.g. QField base maps) had no raster grabbers and rendered nothing
- fixed: features on the edge of a data-derived layer extent were missing from `mapGetFeatures`
- fixed: QField base map rendering failed for paletted images
- fixed: wrong results from `datetimex.difference` with pendulum's compiled extension

## Version 8.5.1

- MapProxy replaced by the built-in raster subsystem: raster layers are fetched, reprojected and cached in-process
- one global tile grid per CRS for all layers and the WMTS service; layer `grid`, `server.mapproxy` and `withMapproxy` are ignored
- `cache.maxLevel` refers to the global grid and defaults to 18; small explicit values need adjusting
- added `cache.name` and `cache.crs` options
- uncached layers keep tiles for 60 seconds, so a viewport is rendered once per block
- raster layers are available in every CRS their extent intersects
- added `display: client` for WMTS layers
- reworked the cache CLI (`gws cache status|seed|drop`)
- HTTP client uses keep-alive connections
- fixed the bbox axis order for box requests in lat/lon maps
- fixed race conditions in directory creation and ephemeral cleanup; file writes are atomic

## Version 8.5.0

- minor bugs fixes and improvements
